hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21490","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid: Abdullah ibn Isa narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I was in the mosque, and a man entered and recited a recitation I disapproved of, then another entered and recited a recitation other than his companion's recitation, so we all stood and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: O Messenger of Allah, this one recited a recitation I disapproved of, then this one entered and recited a recitation other than his companion's recitation. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them both: Recite. So they recited. He said: You are both right. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them what he said, it weighed upon me, and not even when I was in Jahiliyyah. When he saw what overwhelmed me he struck my chest, so I poured sweat, and as if I looked to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in awe. So he said: O Ubayy, my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, sent to me that I recite the Quran upon one harf, so I returned to Him that He make easy upon my ummah, so He sent to me that I recite it upon two ahruf, so I returned to Him that He make easy upon my ummah, so He sent to me that I recite it upon seven ahruf, and for you with every return a request you ask Me. He said: I said: O Allah, forgive my ummah, O Allah, forgive my ummah, and I deferred the third for a day creation shall desire to me therein, even Ibrahim, peace and prayer be upon him."
"21491","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Mujahid from Ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Adaat Bani Ghifar. He said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon one harf. He said: I ask Allah His pardon and His forgiveness, and my ummah cannot bear that. Then he came a second time and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon two ahruf. So he said: I ask Allah His pardon and His forgiveness, my ummah cannot bear that. Then he came a third time and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon seven ahruf, so whichever harf they recite upon, they are right."
"21492","Abdullah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Shubah from Qatadah from Azrah from al-Hasan al-Urani from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar from Ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab concerning this verse: And We shall surely make them taste of the nearer torment without the greater torment. He said: Calamities and the smoke have passed, and the assault and the binding."
"21493","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us from Abu Janab from Abdullah ibn Isa from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me, saying: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a Bedouin came and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have a brother, in him pain. He said: And what is his pain. He said: In him madness. He said: Bring him to me. So he placed him before him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge for him with Fatihat al-Kitab and four verses from the beginning of Surat al-Baqarah, and these two verses: And your God is One God, and Ayat al-Kursi, and three verses from the end of Surat al-Baqarah, and a verse from Al Imran: Allah bears witness there is no god but He, and a verse from al-Araf: Your Lord is Allah who created the heavens and the earth, and the end of Surat al-Muminun: So exalted is Allah, the Sovereign, the Truth, and a verse from Surat al-Jinn: And exalted is the majesty of our Lord, and ten verses from the beginning of al-Saffat, and three verses from the end of Surat al-Hashr, and: Say, He is Allah, One, and the two refuge-seeking ones. So the man stood as if he never complained at all."
"21494","Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi Luwayn narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us: Umar ibn Salim al-Aftas narrated to us from his father from Zubayd from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Adaat Bani Ghifar and said: O Muhammad, Allah commands you to recite the Quran upon one harf, and he kept increasing him until it reached seven ahruf."
"21495","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Ghundar narrated to us from Shubah from al-Hasan from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon seven ahruf, so whichever harf they recite upon, they are right."
"21496","Jafar ibn Mihran al-Sabbak al-Basri narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from al-Hakam from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Adaat Bani Ghifar and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon one harf. So he said: I ask Allah His pardon and His forgiveness. So he mentioned the hadith until he said: Allah commands you to teach your ummah the Quran upon seven ahruf, so whoever recited a harf of it, it is as He said."
"21497","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Two men traced lineages in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so one said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, so who are you, no mother for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men traced lineages in the time of Musa, peace be upon him, so one said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, until he counted nine, so who are you, no mother for you. He said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, son of Islam. He said: So Allah revealed to Musa, peace be upon him, that these two tracing lineages: As for you, O you affiliating or tracing to nine in the Fire, you are their tenth. And as for you, O you affiliating to two in Paradise, you are their third in Paradise."
"21498","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to me: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Isa from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me, saying: I was in the mosque, and a man entered and prayed and recited a recitation I disapproved of, then another man entered and prayed and recited a recitation other than his companion's recitation. When we finished prayer we entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: O Messenger of Allah, this one recited a recitation I disapproved of, then this one entered and recited a recitation other than his companion's recitation. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Recite. So they recited, and he said: You did well. So there fell in myself of denial, and not even when I was in Jahiliyyah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what overwhelmed me he struck my chest. He said: So I poured sweat, and as if I looked to my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, in awe. So he said to me: Ubayy, my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, sent to me and said to me: Recite upon one harf. So I returned to Him that He make easy upon my ummah. So He returned to me that I recite upon two ahruf. So I returned to Him three times that He make easy upon my ummah. So He returned to me that I recite upon seven ahruf, and for you with every return I responded to you your request I give you. So I said: O Allah, forgive my ummah, O Allah, forgive my ummah, and I deferred the third for a day creation shall desire to me therein, even Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
